 R←Test_Select_014(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;list
⍝ Exercise "Select" with `quitFlag` as fourth positional parameter.
⍝ This needs a user; the checks that don't are carried out by "Test_Select_013".
⍝ The parameter was introduced in 3.1.0
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If batchFlag
     R←T._NoBatchTest ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 list←'One' 'Two' 'Three'

 ∆Info'Info: this test needs you: next just press <enter> - must be rejected - and then enter "q"'
 →T.PassesIf ¯1≡('Select or quit:' 0 1 1)C.Select list
 →T.PassesIf C.YesOrNo'Did the prompt offer "q=quit"?'

 0 ∆Info'Info: next enter "q" - must be rejected - and then "2"'
 →T.PassesIf 2≡('Select, no quitting:' 1 1 0)C.Select list

 0 ∆Info'Info: next enter "q" - must be rejected - and then just press <enter>'
 →T.PassesIf ⍬≡('Select nothing, no quitting:' 0 0 0)C.Select list
 →T.PassesIf~C.YesOrNo'Did the prompt offer "q=quit"?'

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
